:: Racecourse
<<effects>>
<<run setup.horserace.ensureState()>><<run setup.horserace.weeklyState()>><<outfitChecks>>
<<if $farm.horseRaceUnlocked isnot true>>
	The fenced-off course is quiet. Alex has not opened it for racing yet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $horserace.phase is "idle" or $horserace.phase is "finished" or $horserace.phase is "closed">><<run setup.horserace.createRace(true)>><</if>>
	<<if $horserace.phase is "closed">>
		<<endevent>>
		<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
		The racecourse is much quieter than usual. A few handlers linger near the stable gate,
		but no bookies are calling odds and no horses are being led to the start.
		<br><br>
		Alex checks the empty course, then gives you an apologetic look.
		"The horses don't look in any shape to run today. Too many are lame or shaken up. We'll have to close betting until they're right again.
		<span class="pink">Maybe we can train them better...</span>"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		The racecourse is already noisy. Bookies shout over each other, betting slips pass from hand to hand,
		and the horses are led towards the gate.
		<br><br>
		<<if $weekly.horseRaceIncidentLossStreak gte 2>>
			<span class="purple">A strange hesitation sits under the noise today</span>.
			A few handlers watch the runners too closely, and some of the bookies lower their voices before taking the next slip.
			No one says the race is fixed, but no one looks comfortable either.
		<</if>>
		<<if $exposed gte 2>>
			<span class="pink">A few conversations die as you approach</span>.
			The bookies stare, the handlers pretend not to, and Alex quickly steps closer as if <<nnpc_he "Alex">>
			can block the whole racecourse from seeing you.<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<<if $face isnot "covered">><<fameexhibitionism 1>><</if>>
		<<elseif $exposed is 1>>
			<span class="pink">Several people glance your way and whisper</span>,
			but the bookies are more interested in taking bets than asking questions about what you're wearing...
			or almost not wearing.<<garousal>><<arousal 200>>
		<</if>>
		<<print setup.horserace.renderHorseList()>>
		<<link "Place a bet" "Racecourse Betting">><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Betting
<<effects>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "closed">>
	<<endevent>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	Alex gives the empty course another look. "The horses don't look in any shape to run today.
	Too many are lame or shaken up. We'll have to close betting until they're right again.
	<span class="pink">Maybe we can train them better...</span>"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	The board changes one last time while the bookie calls for final bets.
	<<print setup.horserace.renderHorseList()>>
	<<if !$horserace.selectedHorseId>>
		Choose a horse to back.
		<p class="horse-race-bet-links">
		<<set _firstHorseLink to true>>
		<<for _horse range $horserace.horses>>
			<<if _firstHorseLink>><<set _firstHorseLink to false>><<else>><br><</if>>
			<<set _label to _horse.name + " (" + _horse.odds.toFixed(2) + "x)">>
			<<capture _horse>>
				<<link _label "Racecourse Betting">><<set $horserace.selectedHorseId to _horse.id>><<set $horserace.betInput to "">><</link>>
			<</capture>>
		<</for>>
		</p>
	<<else>>
		<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.selectedHorseId)>>
		You choose <<print _horse.name>>. Choose how much you want to bet.
		<<set _presetBets to [100, 500, 1000, 2000]>><<set _firstBet to true>><<set _shownPreset to false>>
		<p class="horse-race-bet-links">
		<<for _amount range _presetBets>>
			<<set _internalAmount to setup.horserace.toInternalMoney(_amount)>>
			<<if $money >= _internalAmount>>
				<<set _shownPreset to true>>
				<<if _firstBet>>
					<<set _firstBet to false>>
				<<else>>
					 |
				<</if>>
				<<set _label to _amount.toLocaleString("en-GB") + "£">>
				<<capture _amount>>
					<<link _label "Racecourse Betting Submit">><<set $horserace.betInput to _amount + "">><</link>>
				<</capture>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
		</p>
		<<if !_shownPreset>>
			<span class="red">You do not have enough money for the smallest preset bet.</span>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<steedicon>><<link "Choose a different horse" "Racecourse Betting">><<set $horserace.selectedHorseId to "">><<set $horserace.betInput to "">><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Betting Submit
<<set _betResult to setup.horserace.placeBet($horserace.selectedHorseId, $horserace.betInput)>>
<<if _betResult.ok>>
	The bookie takes your stake, tears off a betting slip, and waves you towards the rail.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Go to the viewing rail|Racecourse Rail Check]]>><<npc Alex>><<person1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $horserace.lastError>><p class="red"><<print $horserace.lastError>></p><</if>>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Racecourse Rail Check
<<outfitChecks>><<npc Alex>><<person1>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "betting">>
	The race can't start until you place a bet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<<elseif $exposed gte 2 and $settings.horsesEnabled and $daily.horseRaceHorseBreakChecked isnot true>>
	<<set $daily.horseRaceHorseBreakChecked to true>><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>>
	Several horses glance your way as you approach the viewing rail. At first, it is easy to blame the noise, the crowd, or the unfamiliar scent of the racecourse.
	Then you notice how fixed their attention is. Their ears turn towards you. One of them stops listening to its handler entirely.
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">Only then does your own nakedness feel impossible to ignore.</span>
	<br><br>
	Alex notices, then looks you over with a frown. "Why are you walking around dressed like that here?"
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		"Sorry," you say quietly, drawing in on yourself. "I didn't think it would matter."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		"It's not your business," you mutter, glancing aside.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"I don't think my clothes are the important part right now, Alex," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I can move away from the rail if you want," you say.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"None of your business," you say.
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
			You make no effort to hide your irritation.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"It's not your business," you say.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Alex opens <<his>> mouth, then stops as a few spectators nearby snicker.
	"Fine," <<he>> says, clicking <<his>> tongue. "Wear whatever you want at the biggest horse race we've ever had. Brilliant idea."
	<br><br>
	The horse that has been staring at you suddenly jerks hard against its lead. Its handler swears, boots sliding in the dirt as the animal surges towards the rail.
	Alex tries to grab you, but the crowd panics and shoves between you.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break]]>><<endevent>><<beastNEWinit 1 horse>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	One of the horses glances your way as you reach the viewing rail, then another. A third starts shifting uneasily, tugging at its lead until the handler has to pull it back.
	<br><br>
	One of the handlers hauls a horse back before it can get too close to the rail. Alex goes pale. "Maybe don't stand too close," <<he>> says, keeping one eye on the horses.<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Watch the race|Racecourse Watch]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Watch
<<outfitChecks>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "betting">>
	The race can't start until you place a bet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderTrack()>>
	<<script>>setTimeout(function () {setup.horserace.placeMarkers(); setup.horserace.refreshLiveView("Racecourse Result", "See the result");}, 0);<</script>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderRaceLog()>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderLiveControls("Racecourse Result", "See the result", "Start watching", "Pause watching", 1600)>>
	<span id="horse-race-result-link">
	<<link "Skip to the finish" "Racecourse Result">><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</link>>
	</span>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Result
<<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<endevent>>
<<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "finished">><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</if>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderResult()>>
<<link "Run another race" "Racecourse Betting">><<run setup.horserace.createRace(true)>><</link>>
<<if $horserace.lossTraumaPending>><<gggtrauma>><<trauma 15>><<set $horserace.lossTraumaPending to false>>
<<elseif $horserace.lossStressPending>><<gggstress>><<stress 20>><<set $horserace.lossStressPending to false>><</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<run setup.horserace.clearRaceData()>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Horse Break
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<beastNEWinit 1 horse m penis beast>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<set $NPCList[0].stance to "top">>
	<<if $pronoun is "m">>
		<<set $position to "doggy">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
	<</if>>
	<<set $position_lock to 1>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<<audience>>
<<stateman>>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Horse Break Finish
<<effects>>
The handlers finally get the horse under control and drag it away from the rail. The crowd takes a long moment to settle, muttering and staring as the bookies shout for everyone to move back.
<br><br>
By the time Alex finds you again, the race has already finished.
<br><br>
<<endcombat>>
<<link [[Next|Racecourse Result]]>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Intro
<<run setup.horserace.ensureState()>>
<<set $farm.horseRaceUnlocked to true>><<set $farm.horseRaceIntroSeen to true>>
Alex leads you past the stable, down a fresh line of fencing where the grass has been cut short and the mud has been packed flat. Workers are still arguing over posts near the far bend, but the shape of the place is clear already: a racecourse.
<br><br>
"I wanted to show you before anyone else saw it," Alex says, unable to hide <<his>> smile. "We've done well. Not just survived. Done well. And that's because of you. The fields, the animals, the repairs... all of it. I couldn't have got this far alone."
<br><br>
<<He>> rubs the back of <<his>> neck. "One of my dad's old business partners helps run race meetings. Transport, bookies, safety checks, all that boring official stuff. We got talking, and... well. They're willing to work with us. We provide the land and horses. They bring the people who know how to make it legal and profitable."
<br><br>
A board has been nailed near the gate. The paint is still drying.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">Alex's farm can now host horse races.</span>
<br><br>
"No pressure," Alex adds, badly pretending this isn't the most excited <<he>> has looked all week. "But I thought we could walk the course. Make sure it doesn't fall apart before I invite half the town here."
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk the course|Farm Horse Race Walk]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Walk
<<effects>>
One of the race horses stamps as you pass, neck arched and ears flicking. Its handler murmurs to it, but the horse looks more interested in the open track than in behaving.
<br><br>
"See? That's what I mean. Farm horses want a job. Race horses want a reason to bolt, and we just try to make sure they bolt in the right direction." <<He>> clicks <<his>> tongue as the horse tosses its head. "Still easier than dealing with Remy. Usually."
<br><br>
<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled>>
	One stallion near the rail goes still as you pass, ears forward and body tense, before becoming <span class="pink">far too obviously excited, its cock visibly erect</span>.
	Another horse at the far end gives you the same fixed stare. Then a third.
	<br><br>
	Alex follows your gaze, then notices another horse reacting the same way. His face turns scarlet. "Right... Brilliant. Great. We're going over there now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> catches your sleeve and quickly ushers you away from the rail, putting <<himself>> between you and the horses.
<<else>>
	One stallion near the rail goes very still as you pass, ears forward and body tense. It stamps once, then twice, making Alex wince.
	Another horse at the far end starts making a fuss. Then a third joins in, tugging at its lead until the handler has to calm it down.
	<br><br>
	Alex looks from one horse to the next, frowning. "Right... Brilliant. Great. We're going over there now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> catches your sleeve and quickly ushers you away from the rail.
<</if>>
<br><br>
By the viewing rail, the handlers are already lining the horses up.
"Let's watch them once," Alex says. "If nobody panics, jumps a fence, or makes me regret this, I'll call it a success."
<br><br>
<<link [[Watch the trial race|Farm Horse Race Trial Watch]]>><<run setup.horserace.startTrialRace()>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Trial Watch
<<print setup.horserace.renderTrack()>>
<<script>>setTimeout(function () {setup.horserace.placeMarkers(); setup.horserace.refreshLiveView("Farm Horse Race Trial Result", "See how it went");}, 0);<</script>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderRaceLog()>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderLiveControls("Farm Horse Race Trial Result", "See how it went", "Start the trial race", "Pause watching", 1600)>>
<span id="horse-race-result-link">
<<link "Let Alex skip to the finish" "Farm Horse Race Trial Result">><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</link>>
</span>

:: Farm Horse Race Trial Result
<<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>>
<<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "finished">><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</if>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderResult()>>
Alex watches the winner by the far rail. Only then does <<he>> seem to remember how to breathe. "Nothing broke!" <<He>> laughs, still a little nervous. "I'll take that as a good sign."
<br><br>
A handler waves from the track. Alex waves back, then turns to you with a brighter smile.
<br><br>
"I'll have the betting board ready next time," <<he>> says. "Come back when you want to watch a proper race. The bookies should be ready by then, if you feel like risking a little cash."
<br><br>
<span class="gold">The racecourse is now open from the farmyard.</span>
<br>
<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<run setup.horserace.clearRaceData()>><</link>>
